summary:
I read the build-3 client at C:\Users\SynAckITPC\Documents\AI\sc-s80-base (origin/main 683f56c0; the session-79 ledger.md:84 records that build 3 was built from this exact commit) and checked it against the deployed root app/ backend.

What build 3 can show:
1. A results screen ALWAYS crowns a winner. There is no response field build 3 can read that hides the emerald winner card or the "Top match" badge (الأفضل تطابقاً). When scoring_v2 is present, the crown comes from scoring_v2.overall_score, not winner_index. A null winner_index or an exact tie still crowns product A.
2. The audit's proposed result `status` values (partial_no_winner, needs_identification, ...) would be ignored: no client code reads result.status, result_status or outcome (grep). So during review, "no winner" can only be expressed as a coded failure:
   - text and URL compares: a 400 with code INSUFFICIENT_DATA, which shows "Thin data on that pair — swap in two products with brand and model."
   - camera compares: the existing `action` values `error`, `need_second_product` or `comparison_failed`.

Which code path build 3 uses:
3. Build 3 only uses REST compare. SSE is compiled OFF (ENABLE_EXPO_FETCH_SSE_DEFAULT=false).
4. Build 3 renders `overview.products`, not the legacy `products` alias. So image_url, category_profile and similar fixes must land on overview.products[i]. Today overview.products carries no category_profile, so the "At a glance" section never renders on a fresh compare.
5. The client renders backend prose verbatim (factual_verdict, delta_text, key_tradeoff, reason, applied_shifts). Only `lang` on GET /text/compare tells the server the UI language. The URL compare body and the camera upload carry no language at all. The factual-verdict templates are English f-strings for both languages (verdict_builder.py:6 even maps "ar" to "If you want"). That explains the English verdict lines and the "Longer-lasting" / "Comparable" captions in the V01 and V07 screenshots, while the dimension labels are correctly Arabic.

Crash risks (render-time TypeErrors from the code), in order of severity:
- a scoring_v2.confidence_legs value that is null or outside strong/acceptable/weak;
- a non-string applied_shifts[].dim_display;
- non-array pros or cons;
- a non-string, truthy delta_text;
- an object-valued overview.winner.reason;
- a non-string history `category`;
- a top-level `result` key added to the /image/identify body (the client would render that key instead of the payload).

Silent misrenders:
- a dimension score of 0 makes the whole bar block show an English "Dimension scored 0 — backend contract breach." line;
- English banned words (better, best, ...) in factual_verdict.line1 make the "why" block blank, because the factual verdict always takes precedence over the localized reason;
- scoring_v2 = {} crowns product 0;
- scoring_v2 = null with `scoring` present renders an empty bordered card.

Two dark backend flags would change what reviewers see:
- ENABLE_COMPARISON_ID_ECHO would turn the text-only share of a fresh result into the referral share sheet. The App Review notes describe the text-only behaviour.
- ENABLE_HONEST_PARTIAL_SCORING would blank the "why" block on partial results.

findings.detail:
A backend fix can localize all of the following additively by changing string VALUES, with no client change:
- factual_verdict line1/line2;
- delta_text;
- key_tradeoff and reason;
- applied_shifts.dim_display;
- category_profile labels (the client prefers results.spec.<key>, 68 keys).

New dimension keys must come from the 51-key catalog. Otherwise the raw backend `label` shows, in English unless the backend localizes it.

On the text path, `lang` is the language signal. URL and camera compares send none, so those paths need server-side language resolution.
